# SABOTAGE: T84b (ADR-044 §9.2) — the cockpit mount's own namespace requirement. The guard CALL
# is deleted from `samen_operator_routes/2`'s macro body (the guard function stays defined), so
# `fleet_cockpit: true` with no — or a `nil` — `:fleet_namespace` compiles again. That is exactly
# the half-named cockpit this task exists to refuse: the label is what
# `Samen.Web.Operator.Fleet.gate/2` hands the cockpit, so the mount compiles, boots, renders as a
# mounted cockpit and reads nothing — a `nil` reaching `Samen.Fleet.read/2`, whose `Keyword.fetch/2`
# SUCCEEDS on `namespace: nil` and passes it into `Registry.read_rows(nil, _)`. Nothing red
# anywhere: the failure is a production request, not a build.
# HONEST DISCLOSURE: the RUNTIME layer (`Samen.Fleet.read/2` treating a nil VALUE like a missing
# KEY) stays intact here, so this patch pins the COMPILE-time refusal specifically — the property
# the macro body owns. The registry-reached positive control and the guard's own unit table
# (including the `fleet_namespace: nil` anti-tautology pin) also stay green, which is what makes
# the flip attributable to the deleted call rather than to a broken suite.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/router_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: NO :fleet_namespace RAISES at macro expansion
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/router.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/router.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/router.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/router.ex
@@ -186,11 +186,6 @@
   Impersonation.gate_socket/3`, wired by T84a).
   """
   defmacro samen_operator_routes(namespace, opts \\ []) do
-    # T84b — the operator-side twin of `samen_mcp_route`'s `:actor_resolver` refusal (T142):
-    # `fleet_cockpit: true` without `:fleet_namespace` fails the BUILD. See
-    # `__require_fleet_namespace__!/1`, called here so the omission is caught at expansion.
-    __require_fleet_namespace__!(opts)
-
     path = Keyword.get(opts, :path, "/operator")
     session_name = Keyword.get(opts, :session_name, :samen_operator)
     include_aggregate = Keyword.get(opts, :include_aggregate, false)
